Add a login page to the beta-portal project in this repository.

Context
- beta-portal is a Node.js application. Authentication uses JWT bearer tokens: src/auth/session.js exports signToken and verifyToken.
- Configuration comes from environment variables in src/config.js (DATABASE_URL and SESSION_SECRET).
- The dev script in package.json points to src/server.js, which is not present in the repository.

Deliverable
- A login page at /login with email and password fields.
- On submit, verify the credentials and, on success, issue a token using the existing signToken helper.

Constraints
- Use the project's existing bearer-token authentication.
- Do not add sign-up, social login, or password reset in this change.

If there is no HTTP server entry point or no user store to check credentials against, report that instead of inventing a new architecture.

Verify with `npm test` (the test script runs node --test).
